  "dom_id": "step-q340782",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "$$\nf(x)\u223c\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of a function from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $4$th cosine Fourier coefficient of $f(-x)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x)\u223c\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(nx).\n$$\n\nRecall that the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $f(-x)$ are\n\n- ${a}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- ${a}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $-{b}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $4$th cosine coefficient of $f(-x)$ is ${a}_{4}.$",
